06226"},"rawMetadata":"{\"compiler\":{\"version\":\"0.8.24+commit.e11b9ed9\"},\"language\":\"Solidity\",\"output\":{\"abi\":[{\"inputs\":[],\"name\":\"IS_SCRIPT\",\"outputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"bool\",\"name\":\"\",\"type\":\"bool\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\",\"type\":\"function\"},{\"inputs\":[],\"name\":\"run\",\"outputs\":[],\"stateMutability\":\"nonpayable\",\"type\":\"function\"}],\"devdoc\":{\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{},\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"IS_SCRIPT()\":{\"notice\":\"Marker used by Forge to identify script contracts.\"}},\"notice\":\"End-to-end demo of the AgentPay flow on Aevum testnet with tUSD8:   1. Owner creates a mandate for the agent: 250 tUSD8 per-tx cap,      1,000 tUSD8 total budget, 7-day expiry, payee allowlist on.   2. Owner funds the mandate with 1,000 tUSD8.   3. Owner allowlists the merchant.   4. Agent pays the merchant 200 tUSD8 (\\\"invoice-001\\\").   5. Owner revokes the mandate; the unspent 800 tUSD8 return instantly. The two failure modes judges usually ask about \\u2014 paying over the per-tx cap and paying a non-allowlisted payee \\u2014 are covered by the unit tests (test_OverPerTxCapReverts, test_PayeeNotAllowedReverts) and can also be replayed live with `cast call` (see README \\\"Verify the limits yourself\\\"). Usage:   export VAULT=0x...          # deployed AgentPayVault   export OWNER_KEY=0x...      # holds tUSD8, pays gas   export AGENT_KEY=0x...      # the agent EOA (needs a little tQDAY for gas)   export MERCHANT=0x...       # any recipient address   forge script script/DemoFlow.s.sol --rpc-url aevum --broadcast\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"script/DemoFlow.s.sol\":\"DemoFlow\"},\"evmVersion\":\"cancun\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":200},\"remappings\":[\":forge-std/=lib/forge-std/src/\"]},\"sources\":{\"lib/forge-std/src/Base.sol\":{\"keccak256\":\"0x926f1c9907b7dadb56dc920ae80dc4